WEBVTT

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.620
Everyone has their own world inside them.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:17.990
Ball-and-socket

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:17.990
Mark of Nobility

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:17.990
Limb Joints

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.210
I'd guess Yoshida's and Watanabe's worlds are very similar to mine.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.770
That's why we get along so well.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.000
But Juri Makina is different.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.090
I doubt I'll ever step inside her world.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.640
Stand.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:40.430
Bow.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.690
He's totally gonna love this.

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.230
You think?

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.400
She was mumbling in her sleep on the train.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.030
So, you see yesterday's?

00:00:56.930 --> 00:00:59.450
Core's lines at the end were so good!

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.910
I know, right? It was so emotional!

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:03.200
Like, that confession scene, man!

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.960
I was crying, the voice actors were so good.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:05.930
And that song was great, too!

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.420
You talking about yesterday's AbsoZero?

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.040
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.670
That scene was super frigging important in the original!

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.090
Hold on.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.180
Oh, here we go again.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:16.180
Nice!

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:20.050
Kyoma, our hearts beat as one!

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:21.370
We're the same!

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.560
I totally cried at that part.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.560
You're so good at music, man.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.940
It was just a nice song.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.570
Yeah, yeah, Mr. Perfect Pitch.

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.070
You people are fucking loud.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:41.200
But, like, that first episode is still the best.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.490
That script—

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.120
Listen to this, Gokkins!

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:43.750
What's up?

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.790
This morning, Ryo secretly changed my ringtone!

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.670
Then her phone rang on the train.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.420
And?

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.840
And then out of nowhere it's like,
“Your eyes make me crazy for you!”

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:55.970
That's on you, I think.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:58.340
I totally forgot I had that song on there!

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.550
Hey, guys.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:06.770
Slowpoke.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.350
Ten seconds isn't "slow"!

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.310
So what're you talking about?

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:12.900
Oh, Makina, take your phone off vibrate.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.190
Huh? Why?

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.370
Wow, boring.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.030
Boring?

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.240
Come on, Gokkins.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:28.370
I like boring. I hate standing out.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.130
Hey, yeah, totally.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:31.960
I get you.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.500
Plus I don't know to change it.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.500
How about I do it for you?

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.380
No!

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.050
Juri doesn't listen to music much, see.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:40.720
Whoa, seriously?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.430
I heard Makina and Goto are dating.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:43.890
No way!

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.710
I overheard some girls talking,
and they made it seem like that.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:50.730
Do you think they've...

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.770
Dude, I totally know what you were imagining.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:55.800
N-Not!

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.020
Nah, totally. Just look at that face.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.570
I think they're talking about Juri.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:02.530
No way. Why?

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.280
Huh?

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.850
He just looked away!

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.420
He must be really awkward—

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.320
I-I need to go to the bathroom.

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.170
Stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid—

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:41.930
No comment.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:43.840
What's wrong with Gokkins?

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.450
Hey, that ringtone
reminded me of something.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:46.560
It was like—

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.020
What do you mean,
you practice every morning?

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.300
I do, man!

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.820
I work out practically every day.

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:55.880
You guys should give it a try!

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.960
No way!

00:03:58.330 --> 00:03:59.480
Nuh-uh!

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.180
There are way better lines!

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.720
Help me out here, man.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.410
That scene from yesterday's episode was way better in the original!

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.180
He just won't shut up.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.580
All right, fine. Let us borrow the books, then.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.230
I actually brought all the volumes with me today.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.120
Let's hang out after school, then.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:15.660
Oh, good idea.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:16.450
I guess I can let you borrow them.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.140
Don't you think that was horrible?

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:19.500
The timing was just too perfect!

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.640
Who wouldn't laugh?

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.900
I totally would.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.070
How about you feel my pain, then?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:25.850
Gimme that!

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:26.850
Hey, stop!

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:29.990
Makina, can I keep your notes
from yesterday a little longer?

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:33.000
Sure, but you better give them back before school ends.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.720
Hey, copying them takes a long time.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.940
What? I take good notes!

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Ringtones

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Custom

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Song_Juri

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Compilation

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Pop

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Jazz

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Electronic

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Music box

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Ringtone 1

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Ringtone 2

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:40.300
Makina, your notes are <i>too</i> good.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.330
And that's a bad thing?

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.820
You've got a song on here.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:42.350
Hey!

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:45.090
Seriously, don't underestimate my stupidity.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.530
You're proud of that?

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:49.620
Oh, did you need me?

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:51.230
Nope.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.640
Okay, in your seats.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.640
See you guys later.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:15.210
Whose is that?

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.260
Okay, what's that cutesy sound?

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.310
Damn, I'm tired. I wanna skip practice today.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:44.160
You always say that!

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:46.030
Off we go, gents!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.610
I don't think he even knew I stuck it on his back!

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.400
No way, it's gotta be—

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.130
Hey, thanks.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:51.870
What's up?

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:53.380
Put it on my desk.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.480
I'm gonna get my phone from the teacher.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.080
She seems really mad.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.870
It was just a joke. Weirdo.

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:03.860
She's always been weird.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.820
She really tried to change when
she started high school, though.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:09.510
What was that about?

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.010
Hey, can you come with me to apologize?

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:13.540
Oh, uh, sure.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.760
This page is really good.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.110
Shut up, man.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:28.610
What scene is that from?

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:31.320
Oh, it's not from the show.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.120
Must be nice to have special powers.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.700
Hey, these protagonists
all start with their powers, right?

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:41.130
And that helps them snag the heroine, right?

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.290
It's not like playing with
my phone will make me popular.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.490
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.910
I mean, are there even any girls at school who like this stuff?

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:47.740
True, true.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.630
That's the problem.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:54.080
Your worlds need to overlap in some way when you want to get close to someone.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.400
Like sharing hobbies or things to talk about?

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.140
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:00.650
Like, Honjo, if there was a girl in class you liked—

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:02.400
I-I don't like anyone!

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:03.900
How would you start talking to them?

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.150
What would you even talk about?

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:08.400
Yeah, I'd be so lost.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.290
Right?

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:13.450
But if you really want to get close, you have to have something only between the two of you, right?

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.460
Yoshida, it's like you're smart today.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.660
What do you mean “today” my dear Watanabe?

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.920
That was a good song.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:22.920
Song?

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:25.730
God, I hate that guy.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.000
He's so gloomy!

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.280
Damn, no one likes him.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.660
Oh, that thing I ordered online was supposed to arrive today some time after six.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.390
Why do you care about the time?

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.600
I don't want my parents to grab it.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.850
Oh, I have to go to the classroom first.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:40.740
See ya, then.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:41.880
Later, man.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.230
So, what'd you buy?

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.290
Not telling.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.540
Lemme borrow it some time.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:46.240
No.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.450
What, you want me to walk around with it?

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:53.550
Juri, I'm sorry about today.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:54.370
For what?

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.450
For the thing with your cell phone.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.370
It's okay. I don't mind.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.050
“Hiya!”

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:04.350
The kendo team shouts really loud.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:05.580
Have you ever heard Gokkins?

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.260
I know, but I'm not going to run down and watch.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:10.560
What, you're not gonna walk home together?

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:12.380
What about you, Mayu?

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.090
What're you talking about?

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.370
Like, Sakashita!

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:15.970
It's not like that, I said!

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.460
You want rumors to start?

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.490
Oh, please.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.510
Juri?

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.510
I...

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.820
I forgot something, sorry.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.490
In the classroom—

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:36.380
We'll be at the McDonald's
at Ohashi Mall, 'kay?

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.260
What was that I heard?

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.770
I thought I heard music.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.270
O-Oh, this?

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:10.780
Yeah, that!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.530
That thing you just played.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:20.030
U-Um, I heard it during class.

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:21.410
Huh?

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.040
You mean from my ringtone?

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.040
Yeah.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.810
It only rang for a second.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:30.800
I-I can pretty much play a song by heart after hearing it once.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.080
It's in the tune of F sharp...

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.500
Hey.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:39.690
Y-Yeah?

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:43.090
Sorry, but could you stop?

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:45.480
I don't like hearing that song.

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:47.680
S-Sorry!

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:52.040
Th-Then—

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:52.570
Huh?

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.820
Can you tell me the title?

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:57.290
Is it a bonus track or something?

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:58.090
Why?

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.820
W-Well, it was good song.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:02.350
I wanted to listen to the whole thing, you know?

00:10:06.190 --> 00:10:09.330
When I was a kid, I used to make up stuff a lot.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:11.690
I guess I missed deleting one of my old songs.

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:13.340
You composed that song, Makina?

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:14.340
Y-Yeah.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.090
Wow! You gotta let me listen to it again!

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:17.100
What?!

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.960
This man is a doctor.

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:47.960
Juri's such a weirdo!

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.870
You're in middle school now!
Stop making up things!

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:52.370
Wow, did you compose that, Juri?

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:54.130
Wow! You gotta let me listen to it again!

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:14.080
Stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid, stupid—

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:38.670
Aki, you can handle your own dinner, right?

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:42.180
Please don't unplug

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:40.730
Yeah.

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.180
Music

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.180
Images

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.180
Other

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.180
Option

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.180
Shuffle

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:55.230
Song_Juri

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:55.230
Makina Home

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:00.800
Juri, would you mind playing that little song for me?

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:03.310
I'm sorry for getting angry, Juri.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.740
You can play your song if you want, today.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.710
Oh, this man's a doctor—

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:08.860
Ah, Mrs. Makina—

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:13.800
You like to dream, don't you?

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:17.580
Your dad tells me you hear
a very nice song in your dreams.

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:21.080
Juri?

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:23.420
'Kay.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:06.700
That's at the station mall, right?

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:09.020
Wouldn't you want to be
with someone from our class?

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:09.980
That's pretty common.

00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:11.090
Actually, it's super common.

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:13.200
I mean, it's super awkward when you barely know them, right?

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.500
Like someone you never talk to in class.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.290
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.260
God, I'd just die if someone like that sat next to me!

00:14:20.260 --> 00:14:22.460
It's like, “Go away!”

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.000
I-I forgot to buy tea.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:26.500
I'll catch up.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.850
Oh, sure.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:37.120
I listened to the song yesterday. It was really good.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:40.270
It was like I could see a whole world inside it.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:42.030
Thanks.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:44.220
It's kind of embarrassing, but still.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:49.490
Also, I think your mom's voice was on the track.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:50.990
What? Really?

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:51.990
Just a little, before the song started.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.220
Seriously?

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.490
Oh, man!

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.410
It's been ages since I listened to that.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.500
There was someone else, too. A guy.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:02.000
I'd totally forgotten! Like, so lame!

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:04.500
Hey, he called himself a doctor—

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.580
Oh, right.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:14.740
I remember now.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:18.520
Can I leave now?

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.380
Also, forget everything.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:30.090
Huh?

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:31.730
It was good, though!

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:33.020
I know!

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:34.620
What do you even care, huh?!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.810
B-Because!

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:38.290
Oh, those drawings on the back!

00:15:38.310 --> 00:15:39.060
Huh?

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:40.590
On the plastic!

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:44.420
You know, the red, green, and purple things—

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:48.990
What did you say?

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:51.170
Huh? There were three bottles on the—

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:51.930
The colors!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:52.590
Huh?

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:54.680
Red, green, purple...

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:05.690
Oh, the colors were in my dream.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:12.440
He's taking forever.

00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:13.700
Let's just eat without him.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.320
Took you long enough, Juri!

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.360
What else?

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.260
Huh?

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.810
What else was in that dream?

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:35.470
Uh...

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.720
Let's see...

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:40.160
There was, like, a robot...

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.110
A doll or something.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:43.090
A girl.

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:44.890
A girl, and I think she was a doll.

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:46.730
Then she met this boy—

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:47.600
Where?!

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:51.890
On this ancient-looking tower...

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:53.080
No...

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:56.970
A-And then they—

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:12.510
I've had that dream.

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:15.520
Ever since I was a kid.

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.320
I had it last night, too!

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:21.290
I couldn't possibly forget it!

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.770
It made my mom so mad.

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.780
She told me to stop making things up.

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:29.630
Everyone called me a weirdo in grade school!

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:31.780
Mark of Nobility

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:31.780
Limb Joints

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:31.780
They made me see this creepy psychologist!

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:33.050
He'd say, “let me hear that song you wrote.”

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:34.750
“Tell me about it.”

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.780
But I didn't write it.

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:41.480
It was from my dreams.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:48.040
You had the same dream, right, Honjo?

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:49.410
How did you do it?

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:50.270
Huh?

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:51.040
I listened to the song—

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:52.040
I get it!

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:54.550
You listen to the song and the dream gets passed on!

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:56.550
What'd you think of it?

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.260
The world was totally different from ours!

00:17:58.260 --> 00:18:00.320
I really like that one scene—

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.390
You know Harmonie's last moments on the tower.

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:04.730
Uh, let's see...

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:07.280
Did I draw it?

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:09.310
Honjo!

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.390
You understand, right?

00:18:12.050 --> 00:18:13.570
What are you two doing?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.460
Oh, I was helping him clean up.

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:25.910
You don't need me anymore, right?

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.370
It's none of your business.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.170
Look, it had to be—

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:03.900
Hey, come here.

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:04.400
Huh?

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:05.460
Come!

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:15.440
Hey!

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.540
Look, man.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:19.630
Don't spread your freaky shit around school!

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:25.630
I'm just worried—

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:27.100
Don't do that.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:29.050
Huh?

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:33.450
I said, don't do that.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:38.160
The fuck you say to me?

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.280
Those were important!

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.660
Don't try to act cool, you freak!

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.000
What's going on?

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:59.150
Like, how am I not supposed to get jealous when you're with some other guy?

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:03.680
Were we ever dating?

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:05.680
Huh?

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:06.180
What?

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:06.930
Nice!

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:12.090
Come on, now. In your seats.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:15.680
Ball-and-socket

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:38.460
Things have gotten really crazy.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:39.960
Oh, the colors were in my dream.

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:42.480
The dream?

00:20:42.480 --> 00:20:44.970
The dream and not this?

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:45.010
Interview_Juri

00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:52.140
Now, Juri dear, would you mind telling me about your dreams?

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.710
What else was in that dream?

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:54.190
Uh...

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:56.480
Let's see...

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:57.950
A robot.

00:20:57.950 --> 00:21:00.080
A girl like a doll.

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:01.860
And she meets a boy, right?

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:02.720
There was, like, a robot...

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:04.240
A doll or something.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:06.110
Then she met this boy—

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:08.720
Are these drawings from your dreams, too?

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:11.450
There were pretty bottles.

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:15.250
Red and green and purple.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.540
Red, green, purple.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.250
On top a ruined tower.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:22.510
On this ancient-looking tower...

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:23.510
No...

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:29.010
Could Makina have forgotten about this second track?

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.510
I'd totally forgotten!

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:32.520
Yeah, she forgot.

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:38.020
So Makina thinks I had the same dream?

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:39.770
You had the same dream, right, Honjo?

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:41.020
This is all kind of dramatic, though.

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:45.030
Oh man. What now?

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:48.320
I really like that one scene—

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:49.860
Stupid!

00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:00.720
I have to fix it!

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:10.300
I should just apologize tomorrow.

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:19.810
Stand.

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:21.310
Bow.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:27.560
You think Juri's still on edge?

00:22:27.560 --> 00:22:29.020
From yesterday?

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:33.550
When did those two hit it off?

00:23:01.710 --> 00:23:04.110
Makina, I...

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:05.610
You know Harmonie's last moments on the tower.

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:10.360
Did I draw it?

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:13.620
Honjo!

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:14.870
You understand, right?

00:23:24.810 --> 00:23:26.250
We're the same.

00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:32.460
N-No...

00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:34.640
That's not what I meant.

00:23:35.250 --> 00:23:37.520
I wasn't trying to be cool.

00:23:45.310 --> 00:23:49.360
Everyone has their own world inside them.

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:55.700
And Juri Makina's world was, well, really surprising.

00:23:57.360 --> 00:23:59.320
But I could get lost in it.

00:23:59.320 --> 00:24:00.700
And I want to.

00:24:02.390 --> 00:24:11.520
Those two tiny hands of yours

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:16.660
Have borne a heavy burden

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:23.100
For long, I know

00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:32.060
You smiled at me back then, sure,

00:24:32.060 --> 00:24:40.600
But I know that later you cried

00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:46.730
On your own, so no one would see you

00:24:49.650 --> 00:24:59.400
But don't worry, I'll always

00:24:59.400 --> 00:25:02.980
Be here by your side

00:25:03.320 --> 00:25:06.600
So don't you cry

00:25:06.600 --> 00:25:13.610
I'll share the pain with you

00:25:13.610 --> 00:25:17.070
I know we can fly

00:25:17.070 --> 00:25:23.050
If it's you and I
